WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:13.110 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  normally new releases  picks the five hottest upcoming games to  talk about but this episode is a major  exception  with the next gen consoles launching  this month it would be a real disservice  to limit ourselves to just 5 games  so strap in for a jumbo length episode  that takes an overall look at november  including next gen launches and more  let's kick things off with the xbox  series xns launch  one of their biggest day one games is  assassin's creed valhalla  the latest in the series takes the  assassin action to the viking era  where you'll lead your tribe as the  mighty avor you'll lead your people in  an invasion of great britain  raiding villages and building up your  own encampments  valhalla comes to ps4 xbox one series  xns  pc and stadia on tuesday november 10th  it comes to ps5 a few days later  on the 12th dirt 5 will already be out  on current jan and pc by the time the  new xboxes are here  but the rally racing game is also a  next-gen launch title  the latest in the series offers tracks  all around the world  dynamic weather and seasons and even  local split-screen multiplayer races  you can also take on a rival driver in  career mode  dirt 5 comes to series x and s on the  10th and to ps5  on the 12th speaking of going around the  world  let's make a stop at the mysterious  island home of the bug snacks  this cutesy looking game is from the  minds behind octodad  and it tasks you with catching the  titular bug snacks as you explore a  mysterious island  it is a ps5 launch game but you can also  catch your snacks on ps4 and pc  starting thursday the 12th and now the  theme song is stuck in your head  [Music]  and now for a completely different tone  with the demon souls remake  the same team that brought shadow of the  colossus to ps4 is added again  with a ps5 remake of the game that  started this whole soulsborne trend  some of the older mechanics are a bit  different from what strict dark souls  fans are used to  but you'll still be face to face with  some massive and macabre bosses  demon souls launches exclusively  alongside the ps5 on the 12th  ps5's other major launch day exclusive  is spider-man miles morales  like the name says you're playing as a  different spidey in this stand-alone  adventure  and miles has his own set of suits and  special powers to show off  including invisibility and bursts of  electricity don't worry if you're not  planning on picking up the ps5 at launch  though  this game is also coming to ps4 you can  take a swing at it on the 12.  let's talk about one more ps5 console  exclusive  godfall this looter slasher from gearbox  is set in a world divided by the  elements of fire  water earth air and spirit you can  choose from five different night classes  as you fight foes and unlock  all kinds of loot as you'd expect from a  game like this  you can drop in and out of co-op with  your friends while playing  as far as consoles you'll only be able  to play godfall on ps5  but it's also coming to pc on the 12th  let's move out of launch day now with  another much anticipated november game  call of duty black ops cold war it's a  retelling of the events that followed  the first black ops game  set during the reagan era expect a  campaign full of twists and turns  as well as all the usual multiplayer  modes plus some new ones thanks to fire  team  and yes zombies are back too you can  experience all that on ps4  ps5 xbox one series xns  and pc on friday the 13th  we can't end this episode without giving  nintendo some love  and luckily there's a switch exclusive  on the way too hyrule warriors age of  calamity brings the musso action back to  hyrule  but this time you'll be playing a  hundred years before the events of  breath of the wild  link zelda impa and the four champions  are all playable as you fight the forces  of calamity ganon and solve puzzles in  the style of classic zelda games  the age of calamity begins on friday the  20th  and those are just some of the hottest  games launching this month  there are more than we can fit into this  video of course so be sure to head to  gamespot for the complete list  as always remember that release dates  are based on retailer listings and are  subject to change  thanks for watching everyone and i'll be  back with a closer look at more november  games next sunday  you

